# Cursor-native agent context

- Allowed under `.cursor/`: `AGENTS.md`, `rules/*.mdc`, `skills/*/SKILL.md`,
  `commands/*.md`, `hooks.json`, `hooks/`, `mcp.json`.
- Do **not** recreate custom trees (`personas/`, `memory/`, `workflows/`,
  `instructions/`, `agents/` as custom docs, top-level `scripts/`, etc.).
- Rules use `.mdc` with `alwaysApply` and/or `globs` — not `.rules.md`.
- Slash commands use `.md` — not `.command.md`.
- New multi-step workflows → a skill via `create-skill-pro`.
- Cross-cutting automation → `.cursor/hooks/` (Node `.mjs`), not ad-hoc Bash.

```text
❌ BAD: .cursor/rules/foo.rules.md or .cursor/personas/
✅ GOOD: .cursor/rules/foo.mdc and .cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md
```
